## ⚠️ Error Handling Strategy

### General Rules

* Always throw errors using custom error classes from the correct layer
* Always propagate errors **up to the calling layer** — never silently catch
* Errors should only be interpreted or transformed in Layer 2 (services)
* **Hooks (Layer 1)**: must not catch or transform — simply expose error to UI state
* **Libraries/Adapters (Layer 3)**: throw native or wrapped low-level errors only
* **Global error boundaries** (e.g., `InitializationErrorBoundary`) catch unrecoverable errors only

### Example

```ts
export class SimpliPassError extends Error {
  constructor(message: string, code: string, layer: string, originalError?: Error) {
    super(message);
    this.code = code;
    this.layer = layer;
    this.originalError = originalError;
  }
}
```

